Subject: [PATCH] Add handover runbook and content-migration script for the
 practice's own accounts

The SQL migrations carry the schema, policies, buckets and seed content, but
not CMS-edited content, uploaded image files, the image URLs stored in rows
(they embed the old project's address), or staff logins.

- scripts/migrate-content.mjs copies content tables and Storage files from one
  Supabase project to another and rewrites old-project URLs. The source is only
  ever read; the default run is a read-only dry run; writing needs --apply and a
  hand-typed --confirm-target; it refuses a target that already holds enquiries;
  it verifies row counts, file sizes and that every image link loads.
- HANDOVER.md: ordered runbook (lock sign-ups, push schema, copy content, create
  the practice's logins, Vercel env vars, auth redirect URLs, smoke test, clean-up).
- eslint: Node globals for scripts/**/*.mjs.

